"""selfctl - Linux SelfControl.

Block distracting websites for a fixed amount of time, system-wide, in a way
that is deliberately hard to undo. No network access, no accounts, no
dependencies beyond the Python standard library.

How it works (see README.md for the full picture):
  * blocked hostnames are pointed at 0.0.0.0 / :: in /etc/hosts
  * /etc/hosts is marked immutable (chattr +i) while the block is active
  * a root daemon re-applies everything every 2 seconds if it is tampered with
  * a systemd timer restarts the daemon if it is killed, and vice versa
  * the countdown runs on the monotonic boot clock, so changing the system
    date does not end a block early
"""

